@page "/"

<PageTitle>Mekanika - Online Engineering Calculations</PageTitle>

<div class="hero">
    @* max-width keeps the logo from forcing the page wider than the viewport - at
       450px fixed it pushed .main-content to 538px on a 390px phone, which is what
       made the whole home page scroll sideways. *@
    <img src="logo.png" alt="Mekanika" class="hero-logo" />
    <p>Professional engineering calculations based on DIN, ISO, EN and VDI standards. Free, accurate, and easy to use.</p>
</div>

<div class="card" style="margin-top: 24px;">
    <div class="card-header">
        <ModuleIcon Type="shaft&hub" Size="medium" Style="gradient" />
        <h2>Shaft-Hub Connections</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="modules-grid">
        <a href="interference-fit" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="interference-fit" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Interference Fit</h3>
            <p>Press fit and shrink fit calculations according to DIN 7190. Calculate contact pressure, stresses, and assembly parameters.</p>
            <span class="badge">DIN 7190</span>
        </a>

        <a href="taper-fit" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="taper-fit" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Taper Fit</h3>
            <p>Tapered shaft-hub connections with standard taper ratios. Morse taper and custom configurations.</p>
            <span class="badge">DIN 7190</span>
        </a>

        <a href="key-connection" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="key-connection" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Parallel Key</h3>
            <p>Parallel key connection design according to DIN 6885. Surface pressure and safety factor calculations.</p>
            <span class="badge">DIN 6885</span>
        </a>

        <a href="clamp-connection" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="clamp-connection" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Clamp Connection</h3>
            <p>Shaft clamping hub design for frictional torque and axial load transmission. Bolt preload and contact pressure analysis.</p>
            @* Was "DIN 703" - that is the standard for shaft collars (Stellringe) and has
               nothing to do with a clamped hub calculation. The bolt side follows VDI 2230;
               the friction model is general machine design (Roloff/Matek). *@
            <span class="badge">VDI 2230</span>
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="margin-top: 24px;">
    <div class="card-header">
        <ModuleIcon Type="gear" Size="medium" Style="gradient" />
        <h2>Gears</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="modules-grid">
        <a href="gear-pair" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="gear-pair" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Cylindrical Gear Pair</h3>
            <p>Spur and helical gear pair design. Geometry, bending stress, and contact stress calculations.</p>
            <span class="badge">ISO 6336</span>
            <span class="badge">DIN 3990</span>
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="margin-top: 24px;">
    <div class="card-header">
        <ModuleIcon Type="bolt" Size="medium" Style="gradient" />
        <h2>Bolted Connections</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="modules-grid">
        <a href="single-bolt" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="bolt" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Single Bolt</h3>
            <p>Single bolt connection design according to VDI 2230. Assembly and operating load calculations.</p>
            <span class="badge">VDI 2230</span>
        </a>

        <a href="boltdatabase" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="bolt-database" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Bolt Database</h3>
            <p>Metric bolt grades and dimensions according to ISO standards.</p>
            <span class="badge">ISO 4014</span>
            <span class="badge">DIN 912</span>
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="margin-top: 24px;">
    <div class="card-header">
        <ModuleIcon Type="ball-bearing" Size="medium" Style="gradient" />
        <h2>Bearings</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="modules-grid">
        <a href="ball-bearing" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="ball-bearing" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Ball Bearing Life</h3>
            <p>Deep groove and angular contact ball bearing life calculation according to ISO 281. Basic and modified rating life with standard bearing database.</p>
            <span class="badge">ISO 281</span>
        </a>

        <a href="roller-bearing" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="roller-bearing" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Roller Bearing Life</h3>
            <p>Cylindrical and tapered roller bearing life calculation according to ISO 281. Supports radial and combined loading.</p>
            <span class="badge">ISO 281</span>
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="margin-top: 24px;">
    <div class="card-header">
        <ModuleIcon Type="spring" Size="medium" Style="gradient" />
        <h2>Springs</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="modules-grid">
        <a href="compression-spring" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="compression" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Compression Spring</h3>
            <p>Helical compression spring design according to EN 13906-1. Spring rate, stress analysis, and buckling check.</p>
            <span class="badge">EN 13906-1</span>
        </a>

        <a href="extension-spring" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="tension" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Extension Spring</h3>
            <p>Helical extension spring design with initial tension calculation and hook stress analysis.</p>
            <span class="badge">EN 13906-2</span>
        </a>

        <a href="torsion-spring" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="torque" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Torsion Spring</h3>
            <p>Helical torsion spring design. Torque-angle relationship, bending stress, and fatigue analysis.</p>
            <span class="badge">EN 13906-3</span>
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="margin-top: 24px;">
    <div class="card-header">
        <ModuleIcon Type="geometry" Size="medium" Style="gradient" />
        <h2>Section Properties</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="modules-grid">
        <a href="moment-of-inertia" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="moment-inertia" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Moment of Inertia</h3>
            <p>Calculate section properties including moment of inertia, section modulus, and radius of gyration for various cross-sectional shapes.</p>
            <span class="badge">Reference</span>
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="margin-top: 24px;">
    <div class="card-header">
        <ModuleIcon Type="info" Size="medium" Style="gradient" />
        <h2>Resources</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="modules-grid">
        <a href="materials" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="material" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Material Database</h3>
            <p>Comprehensive database of engineering materials with mechanical properties and friction coefficients.</p>
            <span class="badge">Reference</span>
        </a>

        <a href="bearings" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="bearing-database" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Bearing Database</h3>
            <p>Standard rolling bearings catalog with dimensions and load ratings.</p>
            <span class="badge">Reference</span>
        </a>

        <a href="about" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="info" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>About</h3>
            <p>Learn more about Mekanika, available modules, planned features, and the standards used in calculations.</p>
            <span class="badge">Info</span>
        </a>

        <a href="contact" class="module-card">
            <ModuleIcon Type="contact" Size="xlarge" Style="gradient" />
            <h3>Contact Us</h3>
            <p>Get in touch for questions, feedback, bug reports, or feature requests.</p>
            <span class="badge">Info</span>
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    /* Fix card height issue on index page */
    .card {
        height: auto !important;
    }
</style>
